WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.096
The famous Southern Song general Yue Fei was young and brave; leading the Yue Family Army, he defeated the Jin army again and again, and the people all called him a hero.

00:00:09.446 --> 00:00:17.150
The court sent gold plaque after gold plaque recalling him; as soon as he reached Lin'an, he was arrested and thrown into prison.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.364
Knowing the road ahead was dangerous, he still returned to the capital calmly.

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:29.418
The powerful chancellor Qin Hui schemed behind the scenes, bent on eliminating this loyal general.

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:38.120
In prison Yue Fei stayed steadfast and unyielding, never confessing to a false charge, as the bright moon shone through the iron-barred window onto him.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:47.134
People lit white lanterns, silently mourning this patriotic general who had sacrificed himself for his country.

00:00:47.484 --> 00:00:51.084
In streets and alleys, everyone felt the injustice done to him.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:58.514
The three words 'perhaps it exists' — a groundless charge — have ever since been a byword for wrongful cases and false accusations, passed down to this day.

00:00:58.864 --> 00:01:02.584
This lesson reminds later generations to cherish justice.

